  {
   "k": "t2ckop",
   "en": "The Kingdom of Greece under the 4th of August regime led by Ioannis Metaxas would see Italian expansionism creep to its borders in the form of ⟦0⟧'s annexation of ⟦1⟧ in 1939. Mussolini, envisioning an Italian puppet in Greece, sent Metaxas an ultimatum in late 1940, which called for Italian troops to occupy unspecified strategic positions in Greece. Metaxas is popularly reputed to reply with one word: \"No.\" However, historical consensus states that he most likely said \"Then, it's war.\"",
